he Manabarbs abilities will resolve first.","oracle_id":"0f1afedd-c60f-454f-b84a-c8117aec0128","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"On the other hand, a player can tap lands for mana, let the Manabarbs triggered abilities be put on the stack, and then respond to those abilities by casting an instant or activating an ability using that mana. In that case, the spell or ability will resolve first.","oracle_id":"0f1afedd-c60f-454f-b84a-c8117aec0128","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The ability will trigger each time a land is tapped for mana. Each ability is separate.","oracle_id":"0f1afedd-c60f-454f-b84a-c8117aec0128","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This ability is not a mana ability. It goes on the stack and can be responded to.","oracle_id":"0f1afedd-c60f-454f-b84a-c8117aec0128","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If any nonbasic lands are tapped for mana while a player is casting a spell or activating an ability, Burning Earth’s ability will trigger that many times and wait. When the player finishes casting that spell or activating that ability, Burning Earth’s triggered abilities are put on the stack on top of it. Burning Earth’s abilities will resolve first.","oracle_id":"21b8192e-46a2-4a6a-abd5-3a074efa30a9","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"On the other hand, a player can tap nonbasic lands for mana, put the Burning Earth triggered abilities on the stack, and then respond to those abilities by casting an instant spell or activating an ability using that mana. In that case, the instant spell or activated ability will resolve first.","oracle_id":"21b8192e-46a2-4a6a-abd5-3a074efa30a9","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The ability will trigger each time a nonbasic land is tapped for mana. Each of these abilities goes on the stack and resolves separately.","oracle_id":"21b8192e-46a2-4a6a-abd5-3a074efa30a9","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To tap a land for mana is to activate one of that land’s mana abilities that has {T} in its activation cost and produces mana as it resolves.","oracle_id":"21b8192e-46a2-4a6a-abd5-3a074efa30a9","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once a player announces that they're casting a spell or activating an ability, no player may take other actions until the spell or ability has been paid for. Notably, other players can't try to tap that player's permanents to stop them from paying {T} or to stop them from producing enough mana.","oracle_id":"3608f1f7-8dc5-4dd1-ae91-c830e1de9529","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This has basic land types, but it isn't a basic land. Things that affect basic lands don't affect it. Things that affect basic land types do.","oracle_id":"74b7fe23-5d3a-4092-8d78-7c0eba8f6f73","published_at":"2008-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This has the mana abilities associated with both of its basic land types.","oracle_id":"74b7fe23-5d3a-4092-8d78-7c0eba8f6f73","published_at":"2008-10-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
